 	</TEXT>
+	<TEXT>
+		<Tag>TXT_KEY_CONCEPT_SAS_MILITARY_ADVISOR_BATTLES_LEGEND</Tag>
+		<English>Military Advisor Battles Legend</English>
+	</TEXT>
+	<TEXT>
+		<Tag>TXT_KEY_CONCEPT_SAS_MILITARY_ADVISOR_BATTLES_LEGEND_PEDIA</Tag>
+		<English>[H1]Military Advisor Battles Legend[\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]Battle rows are shown from the inspected player's perspective: "Our" columns always describe the inspected player's unit, "Their" columns describe the opponent. The dropdown selects whose perspective is shown.[PARAGRAPH:2][H2]Columns[\H2][NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Turn / Year: when the battle happened.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Result: Won / Lost / Ret (retreat: combat ended without a death).[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Est%: simple strength-share estimate from starting effective strengths: our strength divided by both units' combined strength. It is not exact Civ4 combat odds because first strikes, withdrawal, damage rounds, etc. are not modeled here.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Role: A when the inspected player initiated the attack; blank when defending or when role is unknown.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Strength icon b: base XML strength of the unit (no modifiers).[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Strength icon s: starting effective strength at combat begin (with all modifiers applied).[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Strength icon e: ending effective strength after combat damage was applied.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Strength icon m: maximum effective strength (full health, with modifiers).[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Our Unit / Their Unit: the units that fought; click to open Sevopedia entry.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Civ / Leader icons (Their side only): opponent civ and leader; click to open Sevopedia entry.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]PID: opponent player ID.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Cap#: colored capture count from inspected-player perspective. Green = we captured this many of their units; red = they captured this many of ours; blank = no capture.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Cap (icon): captured unit type when applicable; click to open Sevopedia entry.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Hill/Peak / Terrain / Feature (optional, gated by SAS define): plot context where the combat occurred; click to open Sevopedia entry.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Plot (icon): click to close the advisor and center the camera on the battle plot.[PARAGRAPH:2][H2]Strength Color Coding[\H2][NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Effective strength columns are color-coded relative to the unit's max effective strength: white at full, green above 66%, yellow above 33%, red at 33% or below.[PARAGRAPH:2][H2]Sorting and Logging[\H2][NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Click any column header to sort numerically/alphabetically.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]The LOG button (when enabled via SAS define) writes the visible battle history to PythonDbg.log for external inspection.[PARAGRAPH:2][H2]Blank Values[\H2][NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Blank cells can mean the value is zero or not applicable (for example, the lost unit died, no worker was captured), or that the row was not recorded fully for some reason (early version of this feature, bug to fix, etc.).</English>
+	</TEXT>
 	<TEXT>
 		<Tag>TXT_KEY_CONCEPT_SAS_DOMESTIC_ADVISOR_LEGEND_PEDIA</Tag>
 		<English>[H1]Domestic Advisor Legend[\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]The Overview tabs show cities for the selected player. In debug mode, the player dropdown can inspect another alive player's cities.[PARAGRAPH:2][H2]Overview 1[\H2][NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Rel: religions present.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]T: turns left on current production.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Defense icon %: city defense.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Strength icon: defenders.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Occupation icon %: revolt chance.[PARAGRAPH:2][H2]Overview 2[\H2][NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]d: net surplus or deficit.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Food columns: produced food, consumed food, food d, stored food / storage threshold.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Production columns: produced hammers, stored hammers / production threshold.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Happiness columns: happy, unhappy, happiness d.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Health columns: healthy, unhealthy, health d.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Yield modifier icons %: food, production and commerce yield modifiers.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Commerce modifier icons %: gold, research, culture and espionage modifiers.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Trade icon R%: trade route modifier.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Trade icon FR%: foreign trade route modifier.[PARAGRAPH:2][H2]Overview 3[\H2][NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Culture columns: total, threshold, rate, turns.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Great Person columns: total, threshold, base rate, final rate, modifier %, turns.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]#: total Great People born in the city.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Bad-gold %: maintenance modifier.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]WW%: war weariness modifier.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]HA%: hurry anger modifier.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Unhealthy icon %: unhealthy population modifier.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Mil%: military production modifier.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Space%: spaceship production modifier.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Air%: air defense modifier.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Nuke%: nuclear defense modifier.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Espionage icon D%: espionage defense modifier.[PARAGRAPH:2][H2]Overview 4[\H2][NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Founded: founding year.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]POP#: real population.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Corp: corporations present.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]XP: free unit experience.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]SXP: specialist free experience.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Specialist portraits: assigned specialists plus free specialists.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Angry icon: angry citizens.[PARAGRAPH:2][H2]Sorting and Colors[\H2][NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Signed values sort numerically.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Positive helpful values are green, negative helpful values are red, and penalty modifiers invert that coloring.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Zero balance columns can show - for easier scanning, while zero modifier columns are blank.</English>

